WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.691
People sign in to an Orchard Core site on its login page.

00:00:04.691 --> 00:00:08.968
In this video, you see the User Login settings, from Remember me to

00:00:08.968 --> 00:00:13.480
the editable user details, and how an account gets locked and unlocked.

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:22.894
The options for signing in are on the User Login page, under Settings, Security.

00:00:22.894 --> 00:00:27.540
Its checkboxes change the login page and the details you can edit for a user.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.570
Features such as two-factor authentication add a tab of their own.

00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:34.687
The options fall into four groups:

00:00:34.687 --> 00:00:39.361
Remember me, the theme of the login page, local password login, and which

00:00:39.361 --> 00:00:41.610
details of a user can be edited.

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.701
Account lockout is not one of them.

00:00:44.701 --> 00:00:48.926
The number of failed attempts and the length of the lock are options

00:00:48.926 --> 00:00:52.808
of ASP.NET Core Identity, which a developer sets for the site.

00:00:52.808 --> 00:00:55.320
A separate video covers those options.

00:00:59.561 --> 00:01:01.328
This is the login page.

00:01:01.328 --> 00:01:06.385
A visitor enters a Username or email address and a Password, optionally ticks

00:01:06.385 --> 00:01:08.701
Remember me, and chooses Log in.

00:01:09.187 --> 00:01:12.530
The options that shape this page are in the admin.

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:17.247
In the menu, let's expand Settings, then Security, and choose User Login.

00:01:17.738 --> 00:01:20.696
The page lists each option as a checkbox.

00:01:20.696 --> 00:01:23.088
By default, only two are ticked:

00:01:23.088 --> 00:01:28.878
Allow user to be remembered during login, and Allow user to change their phone number.

00:01:33.178 --> 00:01:37.707
The option Allow user to be remembered during login shows the Remember me

00:01:37.707 --> 00:01:39.598
checkbox on the login page.

00:01:39.598 --> 00:01:44.299
A user who ticks it gets a persistent authentication cookie, which keeps the

00:01:44.299 --> 00:01:46.878
user signed in across browser sessions.

00:01:47.355 --> 00:01:53.396
The option Use persistent authentication cookies by default decides whether Remember me starts ticked.

00:01:53.396 --> 00:01:55.465
Let's tick it, and choose Save.

00:01:56.058 --> 00:01:59.586
On the login page, Remember me is ticked from the start.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:02.488
Users can clear it before they choose Log in.

00:02:02.944 --> 00:02:07.267
Let's untick Allow user to be remembered during login, and choose Save.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:10.524
On the login page, the Remember me checkbox is gone.

00:02:11.011 --> 00:02:16.009
With Remember me gone, the option Use persistent authentication cookies by default decides

00:02:16.009 --> 00:02:19.601
whether password and external provider sign-ins are persistent.

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:26.922
By default, the login page uses the admin theme.

00:02:26.922 --> 00:02:31.229
Let's tick Use site theme for login page, which requires an active site

00:02:31.229 --> 00:02:32.851
theme, and choose Save.

00:02:33.511 --> 00:02:37.652
The login form appears inside the layout of the site theme, with the

00:02:37.652 --> 00:02:40.281
theme's fonts, button colors, and footer.

00:02:44.581 --> 00:02:49.638
The option Disable local password login turns off the form for user names and passwords.

00:02:49.638 --> 00:02:53.781
Its hint asks for at least one administrator with a linked account, one

00:02:53.781 --> 00:02:56.201
that is linked to an external provider.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:03:01.591
With an external provider configured, the login page shows only the provider buttons

00:03:01.591 --> 00:03:03.888
under Use another service to log in.

00:03:03.888 --> 00:03:07.497
Without one, as on this site, the page would show no form at

00:03:07.497 --> 00:03:09.410
all, so the option stays off.

00:03:13.642 --> 00:03:18.422
Let's edit an existing user, jamie.chen, from Access Control, Users.

00:03:18.422 --> 00:03:24.492
By default, the User name and Email fields are disabled, and Phone Number can be edited.

00:03:25.347 --> 00:03:29.558
Back on the User Login page, two options make those fields editable:

00:03:29.558 --> 00:03:34.566
Allow user to change their username, and Allow user to change their email address.

00:03:34.566 --> 00:03:36.387
Let's tick both, and save.

00:03:36.853 --> 00:03:41.030
In the editor of the same user, User name and Email are enabled.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:45.804
When you create a user, those fields are always editable, so these options

00:03:45.804 --> 00:03:47.773
only affect existing users.

00:03:52.073 --> 00:03:56.497
Let's enter a wrong password for the user jamie.chen on the login page.

00:03:56.497 --> 00:04:01.093
The page answers Invalid login attempt, and the failed attempt is counted.

00:04:09.179 --> 00:04:11.678
Every further wrong password counts too.

00:04:11.678 --> 00:04:15.808
When the limit is reached, the page reports that the account is locked

00:04:15.808 --> 00:04:20.699
out, and the user cannot sign in until the lock ends or an administrator unlocks it.

00:04:21.154 --> 00:04:26.864
In the admin, the Users list under Access Control shows jamie.chen with a Locked badge.

00:04:27.358 --> 00:04:31.870
To unlock the account, open its Actions menu and choose Unlock.

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:36.578
The dialog titled Unlock user asks for confirmation, so choose Ok.

00:04:37.113 --> 00:04:42.561
The message User unlocked successfully appears, the Locked badge is gone, and jamie.chen

00:04:42.561 --> 00:04:45.343
can sign in again with the right password.

00:04:47.343 --> 00:04:51.517
The User Login page sets Remember me, the theme of the login page,

00:04:51.517 --> 00:04:55.749
local password login and which details of a user can be edited, and

00:04:55.749 --> 00:04:58.416
the Users list unlocks a locked account.

00:04:58.416 --> 00:04:59.923
Thanks for watching.

